A patch to Scratch Everywhere! (https://github.com/ScratchEverywhere/ScratchEverywhere), which is
licensed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 3. This patch modifies that
library, so it is under that license too, in version 3 or any later version; see ../LICENSE.

It lets a program that embeds the library run the project's scripts itself:

- HostHooks (include/runtime/host_hooks.hpp) holds a callback a host can set. Once it is set,
  BlockExecutor::startThread and BytecodeExecutor::startThread start no thread: the hat block
  goes to the host instead.
- On desktop platforms DECtalk was always built in. It still is by default, but a build can now
  turn it off with -DSE_DECTALK=OFF.

It applies to the commit the ScratchEverywhere submodule is pinned to. The build applies it to a
copy of the submodule; the submodule itself stays as upstream published it.

